// Getgud SAT Practice Test 1 — a committed, hand-reviewed selection of
// College Board question-bank ids. Generated by
// `pnpm design:exam --exam=sat-practice-1 --seed=getgud-sat-practice-1`
// against the live SAT question bank, then reviewed against this file's
// `spec` blocks (which mirror the design script's per-module targets) and
// against the domain/ordering percentages documented in CLAUDE.md before
// being committed here. Re-verify with `pnpm design:exam --exam=sat-practice-1 --verify`
// after any manual edit to an id list.
//
// Because every id here is a College Board natural key (see the header
// comment in ./index.ts), this exact test runs identically on any
// self-hosted instance whose question bank includes these ids.
//
// Design notes (see also src/exams/scoring.ts for the scoring-side
// approximations):
//   - Every question in both modules of both sections is scored — no
//     unscored "pretest" slots, since we have no separate pretest bank to
//     draw from and per-instance consistency matters more than mimicking
//     pretest noise. Module lengths (27/27 RW, 22/22 Math) match the
//     official digital SAT's 25+2 / 20+2 totals exactly.
//   - RW layout: domains ordered Craft & Structure -> Information & Ideas
//     -> Standard English Conventions -> Expression of Ideas (the official
//     fixed sequence), ascending scoreBand within each domain.
//   - Math layout: no domain grouping, ascending scoreBand across the
//     whole module (official: "arranged from easiest to hardest"), with
//     SPR items interleaved near the proportional 1/4, 1/2, 3/4, and final
//     positions rather than clustered at the end (see the design script's
//     `interleaveSprAtProportionalTail` and its file comment for the
//     official linear-form pattern this approximates).
//   - `routingThreshold` is a raw-count stand-in for College Board's real
//     IRT-theta routing statistic — see scoring.ts's file comment.

